    "title": "Democrat Challenges Freshman Republican Over AI Data Centers",
    "text": "• Democrat Paige Cognetti is challenging freshman Republican Rep. Rob Bresnahan in a swing Pennsylvania congressional district.\n• The district is fighting data center projects, with communities across the country opposing them.\n• Cognetti is airing a 30-second TV ad criticizing the secrecy of developers, tax breaks, and rising electric bills.\n• The ad will run on broadcast TV, cable, and digital platforms for $200,000.\n• Bresnahan has introduced the Local Control Protection Act to limit corporations' right to sue over local zoning decisions.\n• The bill has yet to move out of committee or gain a cosponsor.\n• Republicans have made protecting Bresnahan a high priority, with visits from Trump and Vice President JD Vance.",
    "summary": "HARRISBURG, Pa. (AP) — Democrat Paige Cognetti is taking a shot at artificial intelligence data centers in her challenge to freshman Republican Rep. Rob Bresnahan, saying “we're not for sale” in a new TV ad in a swing Pennsylvania congressional district where communities are fighting data center projects. The race between Cognetti, the mayor of Scranton, and Bresnahan is considered one of the Democratic Party's best opportunities to pick up a seat in the November election in its bid to take control of the U.S. House and block President Donald Trump's agenda.",
